From: BeeWi BC7PW bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7601sta: stop the idle radio-off from killing an unassociated STA

STAMlmePeriodicExec() turns the USB radio off via RT28xxUsbAsicRadioOff() as
soon as the station is idle and not associated. IDLE_ON() means exactly that,
so an unassociated STA trips it on the first MLME tick: ASIC_RADIO_OFF, the
pending bulk-in URBs are cancelled (the "unlink cmd rsp urb" message) and
fRTMP_ADAPTER_IDLE_RADIO_OFF is set, which makes sync.c and connect.c bail out
of the scan/join machinery. Nothing wakes the radio again, so get_site_survey
stays empty and association never starts.

The test was meant to be gated on StaCfg.PSControl.field.EnablePSinIdle, but
that field does not exist in this source, so it reads "if ( 1". Disable it;
the power saving this provides is the very thing that breaks the link.

--- a/common/mlme.c
+++ b/common/mlme.c
@@ -1471,7 +1471,13 @@
 
 #ifdef RTMP_MAC_USB
 	/* If station is idle, go to sleep*/
-	if ( 1
+	/* Disabled: this test is hard-wired to 1 because the field it names
+	 * (EnablePSinIdle) does not exist in this source, and the effect is that
+	 * the radio is switched off as soon as the STA is idle. An unassociated
+	 * STA is idle by definition, so the radio goes off before it can ever
+	 * scan or associate; fRTMP_ADAPTER_IDLE_RADIO_OFF then makes sync.c and
+	 * connect.c skip their work and nothing wakes the radio again. */
+	if ( 0
 	/*	&& (pAd->StaCfg.PSControl.field.EnablePSinIdle == TRUE)*/
 		&& (pAd->StaCfg.WindowsPowerMode > 0)
 		&& (pAd->OpMode == OPMODE_STA) && (IDLE_ON(pAd)) 
